Removes the report config that cannot work while reward report aggregation is disabled
Original JIRA ticket: IPET-3635

The schema of mst_rewards_points_aggregated_hour and the whole mst_rewards_liability_aggregated_hour table are created by Report\Points::_aggregatePoints() / _aggregateLiability(), reached only through Report\Points::aggregate(). iPet disables that on purpose (DisableAggregate plugin, IPET-2843 - it walks 10 years of history and hammers the DB), so anything the report config declares but the aggregation never created blows up while ReportApi builds that config, on every admin request:
  Table mst_rewards_liability_aggregated_hour does not exist  (Table::initFields -> describeTable)
  Field newsletter_signup does not exist in table mst_rewards_points_aggregated_hour  (Map::initColumn -> Column::__construct -> Table::getField)

Unregisters those entries instead of creating the table and columns for them:
  - the liability table definition, its report pool entry and its admin menu item
  - the 7 event columns only ever created in Points::recreateTable() and never in any UpgradeSchema: newsletter_signup, birthday, affiliate_create, customer_tier_up, customer_tier_down, pushnotification_signup, referred_customer_signup

The remaining points columns come from UpgradeSchema 104/107/1028/1040/1041/1042, so they exist regardless of the aggregation. Custom behaviour events are already filtered by Mirasvit against the physical table (CustomEventColumns::getSurfaceableColumns). "Activity Over Time" bypasses this config entirely and keeps working.

Left with an open upper version bound on purpose: the next release touching these lines fails the build and forces a re-review.

